From bcab7cf0278ca4167bffe30501ca0447ff57ba66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muhammad Falak R Wani <falakreyaz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:06:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] vtls_scache: free the SRP username when clearing a peer

Fedora's curl-8.15.0 backport of upstream commit 7541ae569d82 ("tls: fix
incomplete mTLS config in conn reuse and session cache", CVE-2026-8932)
dropped Curl_safefree(peer->srp_username) from cf_ssl_scache_clear_peer()
while adding the new key_passwd free. cf_ssl_scache_peer_init() still
strdup()s the TLS-SRP username, so the allocation leaks whenever a
session cache peer created with CURLOPT_TLSAUTH_USERNAME is evicted,
removed or destroyed.

Upstream 7541ae569d82 and Fedora's curl-8.18.0 backport keep this free;
restore it to match.

Signed-off-by: Muhammad Falak R Wani <falakreyaz@gmail.com>
---
 lib/vtls/vtls_scache.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/lib/vtls/vtls_scache.c b/lib/vtls/vtls_scache.c
index 6adab68..3e95c10 100644
--- a/lib/vtls/vtls_scache.c
+++ b/lib/vtls/vtls_scache.c
@@ -192,6 +192,7 @@ static void cf_ssl_scache_clear_peer(struct Curl_ssl_scache_peer *peer)
   Curl_safefree(peer->clientcert);
   Curl_safefree(peer->key_passwd);
 #ifdef USE_TLS_SRP
+  Curl_safefree(peer->srp_username);
   Curl_safefree(peer->srp_password);
 #endif
   Curl_safefree(peer->ssl_peer_key);
